tgd web design prototype
========================

A clickable React prototype of three design directions for the web UI
rework, covering the users table, the user profile and the user's
change history. It is a design aid only: all data is synthetic
(src/data.js, generated from a fixed seed), nothing talks to the
backend, and none of it is built into the web image.

Run it:

    cd web/mockup
    npm ci
    npm run dev

then open the printed address. The root page lists the directions:

  A - Console      admin console: sidebar, dense table, filter chips
  B - Messenger    Telegram-like: contact-style list, info sheet,
                   history as service messages
  C - Data desk    query bar, dense grid, profile in a side panel

Every screen has a real path (/a/users, /a/users/<id>/history, ...)
rather than a fragment, matching how the production pages will be
server-rendered. The pill at the bottom switches direction on the same
screen and cycles the theme (system, light, dark). Fonts are bundled
from npm (@fontsource), so nothing is fetched from a CDN at runtime.
